<title>UK: Russia's Novorossiisk oil port reopens.</title>
<headline>Russia's Novorossiisk oil port reopens.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's leading oil export terminal of Novorossiisk reopened on Wednesday after a six-hour closure caused by high winds and heavy swells, shipping sources said.</p>
<p>The Black Sea terminal shut at 2300 local time on Tuesday and reopened at 0500 local on Wednesday, they said.</p>
<p>The Black Sea ports of Tuapse and Odessa and the Baltic port of Ventspils were working normally.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7646</p>
</text>
